    "description": "<p>Waterbury Center for Nursing and Rehabilitation is seeking a&nbsp; cook to aide in delivering quality food service and customer satisfaction.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Duties Include:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>preparation, cooking, and service of all planned meals</li>\n<li>managing meal / tray line service&nbsp;</li>\n<li>general cleaning kitchen schedules</li>\n<li>compliance with resident Diet Orders</li>\n<li>open communication with RDs</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Requirements:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Certification in healthcare cooking (ServSafe)</li>\n<li>Minimum 1 year of experience in large-scale cooking (preferred)</li>\n<li>Strong knowledge of large scale &amp; therapeutic food prep</li>\n<li>Must be able to do some physical work</li>\n<li>Strong leadership skills and a team player</li>\n<li>High School Diploma or Equivalent</li>\n<li>Excellent customer service &amp; communication skills</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Dietary Aide</strong></p>\n<p>Duties include: &nbsp;~sweeping and mopping floors and keeping refrigerators, freezers and storerooms clean and in neat order~daily cleaning of stoves, steam jacketed kettle, all purpose cooker, steamers, mixers, slicing machine, carts, pots, pans and other food service equipment~may transport food carts to resident dining areas and pick up resident trays to return to dietary department~portioning foods for residents~sets up trays and food for residents using food service production sheets and menus for residents of special diets~prepares in between meal nourishment&rsquo;s or other foods for tray service~performs all responsibilities in accordance with established dietary polices/procedures and safety/sanity codes and regulations.</p>\n<p>Hours- per diem&nbsp;</p>",
