    "description": "<p>Waterbury Center for Nursing and Rehabilitation is looking for skilled CNA's (Certified Nursing Assistant) to become a part of our facility&rsquo;s compassionate care-giving team. The CNA will interact directly with patients, providing comfort and transportation, monitoring their vital signs and assisting with daily living needs. We are searching for a dedicated, compassionate and energetic individual to be a vital link between our patients and the nurses and other facility staff.</p>\n<p>Multiple openings on all shifts.&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>Responsibilities:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Assist with daily living activities. This includes delivering meals to patients, turning and ambulating patients and providing plenty of fresh water, as well as extra nourishment between meals</li>\n<li>Help patients with personal hygiene. Provide patients with bedpans, help with baths, shampoos and showers</li>\n<li>Provide adjunct care for the patient, including ice packs, non-sterile dressings and therapeutic baths</li>\n<li>Check vital signs and record daily information in the patient&rsquo;s chart</li>\n<li>Assist the nurses and other staff as needed</li>\n<li>Adhere to professional standards, follow policies and procedures and abide by federal, state and local requirements, as well as Joint Commission standards</li>\n</ul>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Up to date CNA certificate required for consideration.&nbsp;</p>",
